# Playwright rules (sync API only)

- Use `pytest-playwright` with the sync API. UI tests are plain `def`, never `async def`. Create test data through sync httpx or the API adapters, never by clicking through the UI.
- Use one browser per xdist worker and a new browser context per test. Set `browser_context_args`, `base_url` and `storage_state`. The storage state comes from the per-run token file: API login happens once per run under FileLock, and only the login tests skip it.
- Collect artefacts with `--tracing retain-on-failure --screenshot only-on-failure --video off`. In CI allow at most `--reruns 1`, and always report reruns.
- Page Objects declare locators in `__init__`, preferring role, label and test id, with CSS only as a last resort. Each method is one user action, and web-first assertions (`expect(...)`) live inside `expect_*` methods. Use Component Objects for repeated widgets such as `TaskCard` and `KanbanColumn`.
- Tests read as business flows, for example `board.create_task(...)` and `board.move_task(task, to=Column.IN_PROGRESS)`. Tests contain no locators, URLs, sleeps or `wait_for_timeout`.
- If the frontend lacks accessible names or test ids, list them in `testing/KNOWN_ISSUES.md` and use the most stable selector available. Adding `data-testid` to the frontend is allowed only under `testing-modify-prod.mdc`. If you cannot read the frontend source, stop and report; never guess selectors.
- The fast pull-request subset is marked `@pytest.mark.critical`. The `smoke` marker belongs to `tests/smoke/` only. Browser synthetic checks live in `tests/synthetic/browser/` with the `synthetic` marker and run rarely; their policy is in `design/cat-smoke-synthetic.md`.
- Implement drag and drop (dnd-kit) in one helper on the board page object: `mouse.move` to the source, `mouse.down`, `mouse.move(..., steps=N)` to the target, `mouse.up`. Never use `drag_to`.
